      <memberdef kind="function" id="classProvider_1ac2c776b47dc13f0277c0fe628f9e138d" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="yes" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>std::optional&lt; std::string &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::optional&lt; std::string &gt; Provider::getSqlGetServicesStatement</definition>
        <argsstring>(pqxx::params &amp;params)</argsstring>
        <name>getSqlGetServicesStatement</name>
        <qualifiedname>Provider::getSqlGetServicesStatement</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>pqxx::params &amp;</type>
          <declname>params</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Builds a query listing the services the provider belongs to. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Reads the id from the <ref refid="classData__t" kindref="compound">Data_t</ref> payload into client_id, then binds it as a bigint ($1) and as text ($2). The text form is matched against the JSON staff arrays via jsonb_path_exists; owner_id and admin_id are compared against the numeric id. Results from the four service tables are combined with UNION ALL. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">params</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Cleared and filled with the numeric id and its text form. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The SELECT statement, or std::nullopt if no id was supplied or an exception occurs. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Bindings are made into explicit params entries because the two uses need different SQL types. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
